 "rules": [
  "a) O'Neil 8-week hold: a holding up 20%+ within 3 weeks of entry is kept 8 weeks from entry. None qualified (largest 3-week gain: MU +11.9%).",
  "b) Sell: holdings no longer Buy; holdings 15%+ below cost even if still Buy (replaces the fixed 300 EUR rule of 11 Nov; the fast-drop rule and the resistance block were removed on 12 Nov and are not applied).",
  "c) Keep every other holding that is still Buy or Strong Buy, with the same shares.",
  "d) Targets over all eligible Buys: weight proportional to (score - 6.5) x trend factor (1 above the 36-, 50- and 200-day averages, 0.75 above the 200-day only, 0.5 below the 200-day), 90% of the account (OXY sleeve outside), at most 10% per company (excess redistributed), at most 35% in technology (Technology, Software, Ad Tech). New positions only with a target of 3% or more; the rest stays in cash, not redistributed. CAD listings (GIB) skipped. Kept holdings resized only above a cap; freed cash buys new targets in whole shares.",
  "Sector cap in practice: kept technology was 37.4% of the account, so the most overweight kept name against its target (TTD) was trimmed and no new technology (DLO) was bought.",
  "OXY sleeve: kept with its shares (Hold Positive as at entry, -5.5%, no sell rule hit); it is now 7.5% of the account, not topped up to 10%, because kept positions are only ever cut, never added to.",
  "WKL: the build has no trend data for it (no close in the timing input), so it gets the conservative factor 0.5."
